From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christophe Pettus <xof@thebuild.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:08:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/22] H11: accept a direct /Pages dictionary in the catalog

hayro-syntax records whether the catalog's /Pages is a reference or an
inline dictionary; Pdf::pages_root() returns PagesRoot { Ref, Inline } and
the eager page walk starts from either. Core's index walk starts from an
inline root, which has no identifier: it is not deduplicated, its node is
flagged and re-read from the catalog when a page is built, and its direct
kids are found again by position. A catalog without /Pages stays Invalid.
